        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{2}}^{\\frac{e^{2}}{2}}\\frac{2}{3\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}(2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(2 x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{e}{2}$ | $\\frac{e^{2}}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{\\frac{e}{2}}^{\\frac{e^{2}}{2}}\\frac{2}{3\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}(2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{15}\\int_{\\frac{e}{2}}^{\\frac{e^{2}}{2}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}(2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{15}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}Abs(u))\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}2-\\operatorname{ln}1)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}2-0)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
